{"assets":["/editorial-assets/53231c62c83137ec4bd302e271100ae5634a60955ceb8ad332c46ab60b6c9eba.png","/editorial-assets/895a5237b6fd35e6d87c7d7e96412b0d44665c9b8d2ccce81c2ffb4108e9d078.png","/editorial-assets/4bb091c993a4650f33bd356fa44aa305b187fd4af3d3395c86fd8d8ed9944a91.png","/editorial-assets/9e98465443bbb01daf814c1a35aa1cae2d4fe0c047aadf7e363961ff02b73832.png","/editorial-assets/5c10f35a0272449eb602bc2ccaa26828a2e33db8bb0913e44a880062ff168022.png","/editorial-assets/d5b64db4c971e10c04c73d4bbc2a3d32fad8ec5395b727091db52d48d44a0193.png"],"contestId":"500","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/500/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"500A — New Year Transportation"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this problem we are given a directed graph, and asked whether a particular vertex is reachable from vertex 1. It is possible to solve this by running a depth-first search starting from vertex 1."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Since every vertex has at most one outgoing edge, it is possible to write the DFS as a simple loop. Some people used this to make "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/500/submission/9307130"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"very short"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" submissions."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/500/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"500B — New Year Permutation"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Imagine a graph with one vertex for each entry in the permutation, and edges between pairs of swappable entries. It is easy to see that no matter how many swaps we make, no entry can end up in a location that is not in its connected component. We can also show that within any connected component, we can achieve any rearrangement of the entries that we wish."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Since we want to make the lexicographically smallest permutation, we should greedily rearrange the entries within each connected component so that they are in increasing order."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"N"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ 300, so we are not concerned with runtime. One can determine the connected components using a number of standard algorithms (Floyd-Warshall, Union Find, etc.)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/500/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"500C — New Year Book Reading"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider an arbitrary day "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", on which we must read book "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"' be the last day before "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" on which book "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" was read (if there is no previous day, let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"' =  - ∞). Observe that, on day "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", we cannot avoid lifting all of the books read on any day between "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"' and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". If we add up all the weights of these required liftings, we will have a lower bound on the answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This lower bound can be computed with two loops, in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"M"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") time. We must be sure not to add a book's weight multiple times, if it was read multiple times in the interval ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"', "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If we initially arrange the books in order of the first day on which they are read, we will achieve the described lower bound. So, we have our answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/500/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"500D — New Year Santa Network"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"By linearity of expectation, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text"